.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-admin-accounts-activate - Switch a deactivated account back on (write mode, audited)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 admin accounts activate  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Switch a deactivated account back on: it can start payments and write payouts again.
No confirmation is asked: 'rail0 admin accounts deactivate' reverses it.

.PP
A write: it needs write mode ('rail0 admin write-mode on').


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for activate


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 admin accounts activate 019e748b-…
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-admin-accounts(1)\fP
